SAUCEDECK bring-up — 2026-10-18 (host-driven via tools/bench.py, bringup firmware)

== Rework before / during session ==
- Board rebuilt on perfboard from the other session's wiring list (SauceDeck-perfboard-wiring.pdf
  + pasted list). New pin map: see wiring.md.
- Expander changed: PCF8575C module -> Waveshare MCP23017 board (0x27, A0-A2 open).
- First solder had MCP INTA -> GPIO5 and INTB -> U0TXD (GPIO43). Both desoldered (INTB was
  fighting the ROM boot log on TX).
- Mid-session: operator reseated module wires/header -> fixed I2C (see below).

== I2C / MCP23017 — before reseat ==
cmd d (probe 0x20-0x27 x40, sweep idle gap between probes):
gap     0 us, ACKs/40: 27:40
gap   100 us, ACKs/40: 27:40
gap   300 us, ACKs/40: 27:40
gap  1000 us, ACKs/40: 27:37
gap  3000 us, ACKs/40: 27:0
gap 10000 us, ACKs/40: 27:0
gap 20000 us, ACKs/40: 27:0
idle 10 ms, 3771 samples: SDA low 0, SCL low 0
cmd e (bit-banged I2C, Wire released):
bit-bang gap   0 ms: ACK 19/20
bit-bang gap   5 ms: ACK 1/20
bit-bang gap  20 ms: ACK 0/20
bit-bang gap 100 ms: ACK 0/20
-> fault independent of ESP I2C driver. Registers kept values (GPPUA stayed 0x7F).
   GPB inputs without pull-ups toggled every 20 ms (50 Hz hum), operator touched nothing.

